# The committed frontend bundle.
#
# `frontend/dist` is versioned on purpose — ADR 0006 keeps node off the deploy path, so Caddy
# serves bytes that are already in the repo. It is generated, minified output, and git should
# treat it as what it is.
#
#   -diff   a 191KB-long line is not reviewable, and "28 lines changed" in a pull request is
#           noise standing where a real diff would be
#   -merge  git must never line-merge two bundles. The JS is 160 lines, so a textual merge of
#           two builds can succeed and leave a file that still parses and is neither build.
#           (git does try: "Auto-merging frontend/dist/assets/index-*.js" appeared in #93.)
#   -text   generated bytes, never eol-normalised
#
# There is deliberately NO merge driver, and one must not be configured. A content-level driver
# cannot resolve a conflict here: the correct resolution RENAMES the hashed asset and DELETES
# the old one, and a driver can only rewrite the bytes at one given path. Worse, a driver that
# takes a side lets the merge COMPLETE — with both bundles present and index.html naming one of
# them. That is a silently wrong artifact where the conflict would have been loud. Measured, in
# a scratch repo, before this file was written.
#
# Resolve with `make resolve-ui`, which rebuilds from the merged source. `make check-ui` is the
# backstop: it fails if the committed bundle does not match what the source builds.
frontend/dist/** -diff -merge -text
